  "result": "Perfect! All 124 tests pass. I've successfully added payment tracking to the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** - Added two new error codes:\n   - `NOT_ISSUED` - Only issued or partially_paid invoices can receive payments\n   - `OVERPAYMENT` - Payment exceeds the amount owed\n\n2. **src/payments.js** - New payment tracking module:\n   - `balanceDue(invoice)` - Returns amount still owed (total - paid payments)\n   - `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` - Records a payment:\n     - Validates invoice status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n     - Validates amount is a positive integer\n     - Validates date is valid (using `isValidDate`)\n     - Checks payment doesn't exceed balance due\n     - Creates invoice.payments array if missing\n     - Updates invoice status: 'issued' \u2192 'partially_paid' \u2192 'paid'\n     - Returns ok(newInvoice)\n\n3. **test/payments.test.js** - 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Balance due calculation with no payments, partial payments, full payment\n   - Recording single and multiple payments\n   - Status transitions through payment lifecycle\n   - All validation errors\n   - Edge cases (non-integer amounts, invalid dates, overpayments)\n   - Immutability (no mutation of original invoice)\n   - Complex invoices with discounts and VAT\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- Payments stored as array of `{ amount, date }` objects\n- Status automatically updates based on total paid vs invoice total\n- Balance due never goes below zero\n- Payment dates validated with same UTC-based isValidDate function\n- Full immutability: recordPayment returns new invoice, doesn't mutate input",
